WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
A2L refrigerants are the future of the HVAC industry. The AIM Act — the American
Innovation and Manufacturing Act — is phasing down HFCs including R-410A.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Replacements include R-454B with a GWP of 466, R-32 with a GWP of 675, and
R-466A with a GWP of 733. All are A2L — mildly flammable.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Equipment must be specifically designed and listed for A2L use. You cannot
retrofit existing R-410A equipment.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
A2L systems require leak detection systems, proper ventilation, elimination of
ignition sources, and A2L-rated tools and equipment. The EPA 608 exam now
includes A2L content.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
New residential systems are already shipping with R-454B. If you are not trained
on A2L handling you will not be able to service new equipment within 2 to 3
years.

